paneld is MIT licensed; see LICENSE.

It embeds two typefaces with `include_bytes!`, so every binary and every
container image redistributes them. Both are licensed under the SIL Open Font
License version 1.1, which requires its licence text to accompany the font.
Those texts are kept alongside the fonts and are included in each release
archive:

  Inter           assets/fonts/Inter-LICENSE.txt
  IBM Plex Mono   assets/fonts/IBMPlexMono-LICENSE.txt

Kept separate from LICENSE so that file stays a verbatim MIT text, which is what
lets GitHub and other tooling classify the project's licence automatically.
